e Black king on e6, forcing an immediate response. The knight on d6 would be forking the king and potentially controlling key central squares. This forcing move gives Black no time to consolidate and exploits the exposed king position. After the king moves, I'll have gained tempo and improved my position significantly while maintaining pressure.\n\nAnswer: N: f5-d6"}
