 king. The king will be forced to move (likely to d7, e7, or f7), and I can continue the attack with my well-placed knight on d6 supporting the assault.\n\nReason: Q: d1-h5 is the strongest move because it immediately puts the exposed Black king in check. With my knight already on d6 controlling key escape squares and supporting the attack, this creates a devastating assault on Black's vulnerable king position. Black will struggle to defend adequately with the king so centralized.\n\nAnswer: Q: d1-h5"}
