ltaneously:\n- Gives check to the Black king on f6\n- Attacks the Black queen on f7\nSince the king must respond to check, Black cannot save the queen. After the king moves (likely Kg6, Ke7, Kg5, or Ke6), I capture the queen with Nxf7, winning Black's most powerful piece. This gives me an overwhelming material advantage that should lead to a straightforward win.\n\nAnswer: N: d6-f5"}
