n e6, forcing it to move, and simultaneously attacks multiple squares. After the King moves, I can potentially win material or maintain a strong initiative. The Black King's exposed position on e6 is a critical weakness I must exploit immediately. This forcing move keeps Black on the defensive and creates tactical opportunities.\n\nAnswer: N: f5-d6"}
