obility)\n- Controls key squares around Black's king\n- Prepares potential tactics involving the knight\n\nReason: N: c3-d5 is the most active move that improves my piece placement significantly. The centralized knight on d5 will be a powerful piece, controlling critical squares and limiting Black's options. It's more forcing than king moves or pawn pushes, and creates immediate threats that Black must address.\n\nAnswer: N: c3-d5"}
