 can control this.\n\nReason: Moving the rook to c7 is the most forcing move. It attacks the Black bishop on e7, puts my rook on the 7th rank (a powerful position in endgames), and creates immediate threats. The Black bishop will be forced to move, and I'll have an active rook controlling key squares. This gives me the best practical chances despite being down material.\n\nAnswer: R: c1-c7"}
