e play.\n\nReason: Checking the opponent's King is the most forcing move available. It limits Black's options and allows me to dictate the flow of the game. After Bf6+, the Black King must move, and I can follow up with active Rook play on the 7th or 8th rank, potentially coordinating my pieces for a decisive attack. This is superior to passive pawn moves or less forcing Rook moves.\n\nAnswer: B: e7-f6"}
