anced passed pawn could give me practical chances.\n\nReason: I'm choosing **P: h2-h4** because it immediately creates a potential passed pawn threat on the h-file. Black's King on f7 and Rook on d6 are far from this pawn, which means I might be able to push h4-h5-h6-h7 before Black can effectively blockade it. This is my best practical chance to create counterplay in a materially losing position. Passive moves like advancing queenside pawns or shuffling my King won't change the evaluation - I need to create threats.\n\nAnswer: P: h2-h4"}
